# What NOT to copy when this repository SEEDS another one.
#
# `builder-publish` renders a git-provider `Repo` (fromRepo -> toRepo) when a publish sets
# `source.url`, and git-provider reads this file from the source root using .gitignore syntax. The
# Portal Builder uses that to give a newly created page-set repository the scaffolding it cannot
# generate for itself — the release workflow and a CompositionDefinition — without also giving it
# the parts that only make sense HERE.
#
# GitHub's own "Use this template" does not read this file, so the hand-authored path is unaffected
# and still gets the complete example.

# The example chart. A seeded repo receives the COMPOSED chart; copying this one in beside it means
# the release workflow discovers two Chart.yaml files and publishes both, and the example page turns
# up in the sidebar of whoever installs the result.
helm/

# This README describes the template, not a page set made from it.
README.md
